# .cursorrules
[environment]
os = "Fedora Linux"
desktop = "KDE Plasma"
architecture = "x86_64"
python_version = "3.11+"

[guidelines]
- Use Streamlit for the local web UI (runs fast on desktop browsers).
- Use a separate Supabase project for bar inventory and saved drink recipes (same table names as the kitchen app, different database).
- Provide clean, modern UI components with tags for bar items, dietary preferences, and mixology tools (Boston shaker, jigger, muddler, strainers).
- Support both Gemini API (free tier) and local Ollama endpoint (http://localhost:11434) for AI generation.
- Keep external Python dependencies light and standard.
- This is a drink / mixology planner, not a meal planner. Do not mix the two codebases or databases.
